      "The default comfort food of northern China: a wheat wrapper folded around a filling, boiled (水饺), steamed, or pan-fried until one side crisps (煎饺, and the related 锅贴 potsticker). Pork with cabbage or chives is the classic filling, but menus run long: lamb, beef, egg and chive, mushroom, shrimp. That variety is the one thing to watch, since the wrapper hides what is inside; if fillings matter to you for allergy or dietary reasons, ask before ordering rather than after biting. Locals judge a shop by its skin, thin but springy, and by hand-made versus factory dumplings. A dumpling meal is cheap, fast, filling, and one of the easiest first meals in the country."
